= Inside the guild

Every second Thursday at four o'clock, a loose group of engineers, designers and
the occasional accountant gathers around the big table on level three. They are
the Open-Source Guild, and their mission is simple: make the code that the
company depends on a little better than they found it.

New members need no special skills. The guild pairs every newcomer with a
mentor, and the first contribution is usually a documentation fix that can be
finished in an afternoon.
